Poll, not push. PLATFORM.md rules out WebSockets (501 at the edge) and rules out SSE too, since a function is frozen between invocations and can't hold a connection open — anything long-lived is off the table on this platform.

Since `rollup` only changes once a minute (jobs/rollup.md) and `/api/metrics` is cheap (4KB, 30ms — api/metrics.js), have `public/dashboard.js` call `load()` on a `setInterval` instead of only on click/load, and skip the re-render when `computed_at` hasn't moved:

```js
setInterval(async () => {
  const res = await fetch('/api/metrics');
  const { rows, computed_at } = await res.json();
  if (computed_at === lastComputedAt) return;
  lastComputedAt = computed_at;
  render(rows);
  document.getElementById('stamp').textContent = new Date(computed_at).toLocaleTimeString();
}, 15000);
```

The one real fork is the interval: 15–20s gets updates within one rollup cycle without meaningfully increasing load (still one cheap query per tab per interval, no fan-out since Postgres is the source of truth, not the frozen instances). Pausing the interval on `visibilitychange` when the tab is backgrounded is the natural next refinement, left out here since it's additive, not structural.

